# The credentials this box needs, by name. Copy to `.env` — which is
# git-ignored — and fill in the values there. This file carries the key
# names and nothing else, so a fresh box knows what is missing instead of
# discovering it as a camera that never connects.
#
# `Hermes/run-gateway.sh` sources `.env` if it exists, and it is the one
# chokepoint: both units that start a Hermes process
# (jarvis-hermes.service, jarvis-hermes-serve.service) and every
# manual invocation go through it. Nothing else needs to be taught about
# these. jarvis-widget.service does NOT — it starts the widget, which
# needs no credential.

# The RTSP password the house cameras share. It is never written into a
# URL: `.hermes/home/config.yaml` writes `rtsp://admin:${RTSP_PASSWORD}@…`
# and the jarvis-vision plugin expands it when it builds a Camera. A
# camera whose URL names a variable that is not set is dropped with a
# warning rather than connected with the literal text as a password.
RTSP_PASSWORD=
